window.ISSUES_HANT = [{"id":"003","date":"2026-09-25","period":"2026.09.21 – 2026.09.27","title":"全球女性權益週報：從天皇繼承到土地所有權，平等仍是進行時","summary":"本期聚焦日本皇位繼承性別壁壘、尼泊爾女性土地權利、厄瓜多爾殺害女性、加納憲法改革爭議、聯合國性別平等報告等12條新聞，覆蓋東亞、南亞、拉美、非洲、北美、歐洲、中東、全球與東南亞，呈現政策進步與制度慣性並存的複雜圖景。","en":{"title":"Global Women's Rights Weekly: From Imperial Succession to Land Rights, Equality Is Still in Progress","summary":"This edition covers Japan's imperial gender gap, Nepali women's land rights, femicide in Ecuador, Ghana's constitutional reform dispute, and a UN gender equality report, among 12 stories across East Asia, South Asia, Latin America, Africa, North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Southeast Asia."},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png","watch":{"name":"Nágila Brito","name_en":"Nágila Brito","role":"女性權利倡導者","role_en":"Women's rights advocate","region":"巴西","why":"因在維護婦女權益領域的長期行動獲得“不朽者”稱號，代表巴西基層女性權利倡導力量。她的工作讓地方層面的援助與抗爭被看到，是社區正義的具體推動者。","why_en":"Honored with the title of “Immortal” for her long-standing work defending women's rights in Brazil, she represents grassroots advocacy that brings local struggles into view.","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxOLVlzc3YtemxicUVRR3BpZ3N6bl9lc0hDZ2ZHVGtCWmJOVXZnUDdPRTdaTkNIQzhQRjhSeF85V2dOd2VFbV9wWHd1anpCM3FRTzRnY1owMm1HTEhUZU9wQnZSRkNTTFNQbzFLNktZNU01NDJRNEdqOTJxR2pfQ0ZSRnRZNExuVHdFbU9ZbzJGd2wwcFRTbkJVcGdJT3YtX01LMjBIUkdvNFdYUnV5UXB4SWJJQXpVTWlNQ0E?oc=5","img":""},"picks":{"film":"墜落的審判","book":"厭女","art":"弗裡達·卡羅"},"sections":[{"cat":"國際","en_cat":"International","items":[{"id":"003-1","t":"聯合國報告：全球性別平等嚴重偏離軌道","d":"聯合國最新報告顯示全球性別平等進展嚴重滯後，若按當前速度，實現性別平等目標遙遙無期，需採取更有力行動。","body":["聯合國發佈報告指出，全球性別平等進程嚴重偏離軌道，現有努力不足以按時實現可持續發展目標中的性別平等。報告措辭直接，罕見地使用“嚴重偏離軌道”來描述現狀，透露出國際社會對進展緩慢的擔憂。","報告提到多項目標進展緩慢，受疫情、衝突和經濟下行影響，女性在就業、教育、安全等領域差距回潮。此前有報道稱按現有速度，實現性別平等可能要等到2197年，遠晚於2030年的承諾。","國際社會的承諾與投入之間存在巨大差距。若性別平等被持續推遲，社會整體發展潛力也將受損。報告提醒，危機往往首先壓縮女性在教育、就業和安全上的資源，而不僅僅是統計數字的回落。"],"why":"報告用了“嚴重偏離軌道”這樣少見的措辭，說明國際目標的實際進展比想像中更差。","en":{"t":"UN report says gender equality is woefully off track","d":"A new UN report finds global progress toward gender equality is far behind schedule.","body":["The UN reports that gender equality is woefully off track, with multiple targets lagging. Crises have worsened women's situations in employment, education, and safety.","Without accelerated action, equality remains a distant goal. The report calls for stronger commitment and notes that current efforts are insufficient for the 2030 agenda."]},"img":"assets/img/podium.png","src":"news.un.org","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiV0FVX3lxTE9CRWFIZzY1S1RaczVwZnF5d3g2Y2NzN0dEcXZ0VXAzRjNPVTFfc3JIVkhlSXVYdUhJcVhNRkp0SldLbExydXNQS1JMWXJxYl9XT3FKOV91MA?oc=5","region":"全球"}]},{"cat":"政策與法律","en_cat":"Policy & Law","items":[{"id":"003-2","t":"女性可當首相卻難承天皇位：日本皇位繼承的性別壁壘","d":"日本評論家島田裕巳指出，即便女性可任首相，現行皇室典範仍將愛子公主排除在天皇繼承序列之外。圍繞女性天皇的討論被政治因素長期擱置，折射法律與習俗的性別歧視。","body":["日本政壇已有女性出任首相的現實，但皇室繼承仍受限於只允許男性天皇的《皇室典範》。評論家島田裕巳指出，愛子公主被排除在繼承序列之外，這種反差暴露出制度深處的不平等。","日本《皇室典範》規定皇位由男性皇族繼承，女性婚後需脫離皇籍。近年來皇族人數減少，民眾對女性天皇接受度較高，但保守政治力量仍以傳統為由拒絕修法，將問題長期擱置。","將女性排除在最高象徵職位之外，顯示法律性別平等的侷限。即使女性可擔任行政首腦，象徵性權力仍保留給男性，反映制度慣性對性別進步的制約。"],"why":"女性已能出任首相，但愛子仍被排除在天皇繼承序列之外，這種反差很少被放在一起比較。","en":{"t":"Women can be prime minister but Princess Aiko cannot be emperor: Japan's imperial gender gap","d":"A commentator highlights the contradiction between women reaching political leadership and the male-only imperial succession law.","body":["Japan has seen women assume the prime ministership, yet Princess Aiko remains excluded from the imperial line under current law. The male-only succession rule persists, setting the symbolic head of state apart from political progress.","The debate over female emperors faces resistance from conservative forces, even as public support is high. The gap reveals how legal inequality can survive in symbolic institutions."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png","src":"Yahoo!ニュース","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiAFBVV95cUxPaWszblEwTmxBbDV2VThjMmhrVHJRNVFSWUJha3lCaHRMbUxjeExfdWU3SW1TWWVoaG4wdTFQeGxPcjJQd3ZIZzRHWjd2d2ZZU1VKRTBoM0xWQW85azJNTXFKY244NjNCdTV2TnNkQ3Y2cFRHZDRJeWNhVlAzOG96WTljdUlrNWJN?oc=5","region":"東亞"},{"id":"003-3","t":"加納婦女團體拒絕憲法審查中的性別平等改革方案","d":"加納婦女團體對憲法審查中涉及性別平等的改革條款表達拒絕，認為現有方案未能回應女性實際訴求，甚至可能弱化已有保障。","body":["加納進行憲法審查期間，婦女團體公開反對某些性別平等改革建議，擔心條文表述損害女性權益。她們認為改革方向與女性實際需求相悖，因此選擇拒絕而非默認接受。","加納憲法已確認性別平等原則，但習慣法在婚姻、繼承等領域與成文法並存，婦女團體長期呼籲統一法律標準。改革草案若未能消除這種並行，反而可能讓習慣法獲得更大空間。","法律改革若缺乏女性群體實質參與，容易出現形式上平等、實踐中倒退的結果。婦女團體的反對是一種監督，提醒決策者不能只看條文辭令，還要看女性在日常生活中的真實處境。"],"why":"憲法審查本應是擴大平等的機會，婦女團體卻站出來拒絕改革方向，這種反向動作值得追問。","en":{"t":"Ghanaian women's groups reject gender equality reforms in constitutional review","d":"Women's groups are pushing back against proposed constitutional reforms they say fail to protect women's rights.","body":["During Ghana's constitutional review, women's groups have rejected certain gender equality proposals, warning they may weaken protections.","Statutory and customary law coexist, and women have long demanded alignment. The groups see the draft as insufficient or harmful."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png","src":"Ghana News Agency","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxObS1PMzlUSzh2RFh4MzVwU1p1SGRQVVFMZTNVNjRCajZtQS1wREtzOVM5Y1J5bEN0aVkya1RFRHZoSGZHZHJ0cFNFSjVCdi1YemJBaHdyN2Mzbmg2MG1ILXd0Vk1vZmprcHhnRm5MaEVCLWRvQ3RjR29nckNpWW8xM1l6bHZqa2VqQ2o2VkFEVEpLbS1ZTnV4ZkNEM0FkUQ?oc=5","region":"非洲"},{"id":"003-4","t":"英自由民主黨在女性權利議題上被批懦弱","d":"英國自由民主黨在跨性別與女性權利等議題上的立場遭批評，被指回避明確原則，在核心性別議題上表現軟弱。","body":["有評論批評英國自由民主黨在女性權利相關問題上態度含糊，尤其是在跨性別政策與單性別空間爭論中缺乏決斷。該黨被指不敢明確表態，以免失去部分選民。","英國圍繞性別承認法、體育與監獄中的性別分類長期爭議，政黨常因擔心疏遠部分選民而回避立場。這種政治計算使女性權利與跨性別權益之間的公共討論更加極化。","政黨若在女性權利與跨性別權益之間選擇模糊，可能兩頭不討好，也讓基層女性感到被忽視。清晰立場不只是政治責任，也關係到公共政策的可預期性。"],"why":"一個自稱自由主義的政黨在女性權利上不敢表態，這種反差暴露出政治計算優先於原則。","en":{"t":"UK Lib Dems accused of cowardice on women's rights","d":"Critics say the Liberal Democrats have avoided clear positions on contested gender and women's rights issues.","body":["The UK Liberal Democrats face criticism for vague stances on women's rights, especially around transgender policy and single-sex spaces.","Party caution on contested issues may alienate both sides. Observers argue clarity is needed for trust."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png","src":"telegraph.co.uk","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxPYll3RVdQMGZNdERqTElPd01peEd1ZGtVOXc1RGpZYm1MSjVvNUhMUGJ4dzIwTEg2U1VQOVQwd0lXWm9sMldxSFVnaGNoZkJjcjUtdDRQX25nb0F4REZQV3NxZkpWU2NOZTRhNWszTVFJZk1zaVhmZWI1Ml8xRGIxQ3VhZGZzekE1S2c?oc=5","region":"歐洲"},{"id":"003-5","t":"埃及全國婦女委員會稱婦女權利立法取得重要進展","d":"埃及全國婦女委員會表示，在保護婦女權益相關法律文件中取得重要立法突破，涉及針對性暴力與家庭關係等領域的保障強化。","body":["埃及全國婦女委員會宣佈在維護婦女權益的法律領域出現重要進展，稱多項相關文件得到推進。官方機構主動強調立法成績，試圖展現國家在婦女權利方面的努力。","埃及近年修訂部分法律，對性騷擾、女性割禮等作出更嚴厲規定，但執法與社會汙名仍是挑戰。許多女性仍不敢報案，法律條文與日常保護之間存在落差。","官方機構主動強調立法成績，既可能是真實進步，也可能服務於國際形象。需要觀察法律能否轉化為日常保護，而非只停留在紙面上的進步敘事。"],"why":"婦女委員會把多項法律修改稱為“重要立法突破”，但具體細節和落實成效仍待檢驗。","en":{"t":"Egypt's National Council for Women reports legislative progress","d":"The state women's body highlights advances in laws protecting women's rights.","body":["Egypt's National Council for Women says important legislative progress has been made in files related to women's protection.","Past reforms targeted harassment and FGM, but enforcement and stigma remain. The announcement may signal both reform and image-building."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png","src":"صدى البلد","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiR0FVX3lxTE9kNE5ia1c3a0Izd0ZDUG5nbDVneHplQzZXenJvUkdCU3hYSFhkX0EyWnRCSWpOeXNOSy1sYzA1cF9TWEJxMVJZ?oc=5","region":"中東"}]},{"cat":"社會","en_cat":"Society","items":[{"id":"003-6","t":"尼泊爾女性爭取所耕種土地的所有權","d":"尼泊爾許多女性長期從事農業生產，卻因法律與社會慣例無法擁有土地。她們正推動土地所有權改革，以保障生計、借貸和家庭決策地位。","body":["尼泊爾農村女性承擔主要農作勞動，但土地登記多在男性名下。報道指出，女性希望獲得她們實際耕種土地的所有權，以改變依附狀態，而不是繼續只出力不落名。","尼泊爾法律近年雖有賦予女性財產權的條款，但執行受父權習俗、文件缺失與意識不足阻礙。土地是獲得貸款、參與村務的基礎資源，沒有地契，女性往往被排除在公共事務之外。","土地所有權不只關乎財產，還直接影響女性在家庭與社區中的議價能力，是打破貧困循環和性別從屬的關鍵。當女性擁有土地，她們更可能投資子女教育並參與決策。"],"why":"她們每天都在土地上勞作，卻不能以自己名義登記產權，這種反差常被髮展議題忽略。","en":{"t":"Nepali women seek ownership of the land they farm","d":"Women who till the land are demanding legal recognition as owners to secure livelihoods and standing.","body":["Women in Nepal do much of the agricultural work yet rarely hold land titles. They are pressing for ownership rights over the fields they cultivate.","Though laws grant women property rights, patriarchal customs and weak implementation keep land in men's names. Ownership is key to credit, autonomy, and local influence."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png","src":"news - Mongabay","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","region":"南亞"},{"id":"003-7","t":"厄瓜多爾為何難以遏制殺害女性案件","d":"厄瓜多爾殺害女性案件頻發，儘管法律已設立相關罪名，執法與預防仍存在斷層。報道探討暴力高發背後的制度失效與性別偏見。","body":["厄瓜多爾近年將殺害女性列為特定犯罪，但案件數量仍令人擔憂。報道追問，為何法律明確後女性仍不安全，問題顯然不止於立法層面。","拉美地區長期存在高謀殺率與性別暴力文化，警方與司法系統常輕視家庭暴力報案，預防措施和庇護資源不足。許多女性在遇害前已多次求助，卻未被認真對待。","僅將行為入罪不夠，若報案不被認真對待、施害者鮮少受罰，法律威懾力有限。殺害女性是性別不平等的極端表現，需要從執法與預防同時著手。"],"why":"法律已經將殺害女性單獨立罪，但女性被殺的數量仍然沒有降下來，說明問題不止於立法。","en":{"t":"Why Ecuador struggles to stop femicide","d":"Despite criminalizing femicide, Ecuador continues to see high rates of deadly violence against women.","body":["Ecuador has made femicide a distinct crime, yet killings of women remain alarming. Gaps in enforcement and prevention are under scrutiny.","Gender-based violence is widespread, and authorities often downplay domestic violence reports. Without protection and accountability, the law's impact is limited."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png","src":"DW.com","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTFA5Q2pSMWN5UGZjYUpKRTNDRXBCMURPbVZjRVdqV3dscS1wWTMtU09DZXZ2OTE1YmQyQUhTUWVZMHlPSWFzRDJWTTRLb3NSSFNISGpyNnpPUzlTdnMyd2VsdWRIcFZNRGpZdUJIYkhHOVNuaVVINlE?oc=5","region":"拉美"},{"id":"003-8","t":"加拿大原住民婦女宣言：保護女性與土地免受大型項目暴力","d":"加拿大原住民婦女發佈宣言，將大型開發項目帶來的環境破壞與針對原住民婦女的暴力聯繫起來，要求停止掠奪性開發。","body":["UBCIC發佈婦女宣言，指出大型項目在破壞土地的同時，也加劇針對原住民婦女的暴力風險。她們把土地權利與人身安全視為一體，認為不能只保護土地而不保護土地上的人。","加拿大原住民婦女長期面臨高暴力風險，資源開採項目常帶來外來工人、治安惡化和社區失序，已有調查關注失蹤與被謀殺原住民婦女。宣言將環境正義與性別正義相結合。","將環境正義與性別正義結合，挑戰了將經濟發展置於社區安全之上的邏輯，也提醒主流女權運動不應忽視原住民女性。破壞土地和傷害婦女常常來自同一套掠奪邏輯。"],"why":"宣言把土地破壞和婦女暴力放在同一個框架裡，這在大型項目爭議中並不常見。","en":{"t":"Indigenous women's declaration in Canada links land protection to ending violence","d":"UBCIC women connect major project violence to harms against Indigenous women and demand land protections.","body":["The UBCIC Women's Declaration says large projects on Indigenous lands worsen violence against women. It ties environmental destruction to community safety.","The declaration challenges both resource extraction and the neglect of missing and murdered Indigenous women, joining gender and land justice."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png","src":"ubcic.bc.ca","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxNV1RlQmpSVXV3MkpWMVEzd21HRmJJUTVFUGVVNTJZQ054NGduTE1KSFNtTFVNZjhjVmtBYmk4cEpiVFlfZVJFUWc3SnJEUWNDWVBpSEFFTjlleVFuRGZzZXhpYjVaU2pOdVVqeUlTei1NZU1kOGpJZVBTcVZYNWRpSUNaMU1xOFdTSzl3?oc=5","region":"北美"}]},{"cat":"健康與權益","en_cat":"Health & Rights","items":[{"id":"003-9","t":"墨西哥瓜納華托州尋求強化產婦權利保護","d":"墨西哥瓜納華托州擬加強女性在孕產期間的權利保障，涉及醫療與勞動保護，旨在減少孕期歧視和健康風險。","body":["墨西哥瓜納華托州提出或討論加強女性在生育期間的權益保護，重點是孕產期女性的醫療和勞動保障。保護懷孕和生育期間的權利，聽起來基礎，卻仍需要地方立法來強調。","墨西哥女性在懷孕期間常面臨職場歧視、解僱風險與醫療條件不足，孕產婦健康不平等問題突出。許多女性因擔心失去工作而不敢懷孕或不敢休產假。","將保護從紙面落實到醫療與勞動實踐，是保障女性生育自主與身體權利的基礎。如果孕期被解僱、產檢資源不足等問題持續存在，那麼法律上的平等就是空話。"],"why":"保護女性在懷孕和生育期間的權利，聽起來基礎，卻仍需要地方立法來強調，說明執行很薄弱。","en":{"t":"Guanajuato seeks stronger protections for women during maternity","d":"Mexican state moves to reinforce rights for women during pregnancy and maternity.","body":["Guanajuato is working to strengthen protections for women's rights during maternity, including healthcare and labor safeguards.","Pregnancy-related discrimination and unequal maternal care remain challenges. The effort aims to turn legal rights into practice."]},"img":"assets/img/body-choice.png","src":"MILENIO","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","region":"拉美"}]},{"cat":"文化","en_cat":"Culture","items":[{"id":"003-10","t":"巴西女性權利倡導者Nágila Brito獲“不朽”稱號","d":"巴西女性權利捍衛者Nágila Brito因其在維護婦女權益方面的行動獲得榮譽稱號，表彰她在相關領域的長期投入。","body":["Nágila Brito 因在維護女性權利方面的突出行動獲得“不朽者”稱號。這一榮譽來自巴西相關機構，用以表彰她在女性權益領域的持續努力。","巴西女性面臨高暴力率與政治代表不足，許多地方行動者在基層提供法律援助與庇護。Nágila Brito 的工作屬於這種社區層面的日常抗爭，未必出現在全國性頭條中。","對基層女性權利倡導者的認可，有助於將關注引向日常實踐而非僅法律條文。當一位並非全國知名的人物獲得稱號，地方層面的努力就被看見了。"],"why":"一位並非全國知名的女性權利行動者獲得“不朽”稱號，說明地方層面的努力被看見。","en":{"t":"Brazilian women's rights advocate Nágila Brito receives title","d":"Nágila Brito is honored for her work defending women's rights in Brazil.","body":["Nágila Brito received an \"Immortal\" title for her advocacy for women's rights. The honor recognizes grassroots commitment.","Her work highlights the role of local defenders in a country with high gender violence and underrepresentation."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png","src":"Taktá No AR","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxOLVlzc3YtemxicUVRR3BpZ3N6bl9lc0hDZ2ZHVGtCWmJOVXZnUDdPRTdaTkNIQzhQRjhSeF85V2dOd2VFbV9wWHd1anpCM3FRTzRnY1owMm1HTEhUZU9wQnZSRkNTTFNQbzFLNktZNU01NDJRNEdqOTJxR2pfQ0ZSRnRZNExuVHdFbU9ZbzJGd2wwcFRTbkJVcGdJT3YtX01LMjBIUkdvNFdYUnV5UXB4SWJJQXpVTWlNQ0E?oc=5","region":"拉美"}]},{"cat":"生育權利","en_cat":"Reproductive Rights","items":[{"id":"003-11","t":"生育權利倒退之際，美國郵政發行紀念作家朱厄特郵票","d":"美國郵政在生育權利受挫背景下發行紀念作家薩拉·奧恩·朱厄特的郵票，她曾描繪女性在婚姻之外的生活可能。","body":["美國生育權利面臨倒退，此時美國郵政發行紀念作家 Sarah Orne Jewett 的郵票。她以描寫女性獨立生活而知名，作品展現女性不依附婚姻的可能性。","美國多州限制墮胎後，女性自主選擇空間縮小。朱厄特的作品提醒人們，女性可以擁有生育之外的人生道路，這種文學想像在當下具有現實意義。","一枚郵票在此時出現，既是對女性文學傳統的肯定，也提醒公眾生育自主與女性生活道路選擇密切相關。當法律收緊時，文化表達成為另一種抵抗。"],"why":"在生育權利被壓縮的時候發行紀念一位書寫女性不婚生活的作家郵票，時機本身就像一種表態。","en":{"t":"Amid reproductive rollbacks, USPS honors author Sarah Orne Jewett","d":"A new stamp honors a writer who imagined women's lives beyond marriage as reproductive rights are curtailed.","body":["The USPS has issued a stamp for Sarah Orne Jewett, known for depicting women's independent lives. It comes amid reproductive rights rollbacks.","The stamp highlights literary visions of female autonomy at a time when bodily self-determination is under legal attack."]},"img":"assets/img/body-choice.png","src":"Ms. Magazine","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxOZjhiVWMwZU1ISnIyWmcxTUpEcHhPX0VJQTNZdThjQXZUdmFEdEVWRFNDUmxJRmVwcmFlRHJJY254WGkyTGlQZEVfZjRPQ0lsYnFjRXJTTDUzMUdtd3lhaU00MDk0MGJ0V3o1UGtncGtBVkFaTmVLTWZVYzBid0tmdlZtdy0?oc=5","region":"北美"}]},{"cat":"職場平等","en_cat":"Workplace Equality","items":[{"id":"003-12","t":"提高女性在軍隊中的工作效能以推動性別平等","d":"東南亞地區討論提高女性在軍隊環境中的工作效能，以促進軍隊內部性別平等與女性職業發展。","body":["有報道關注如何提高女性在軍隊中的工作效能，以推動軍事環境中的性別平等和女性進步。軍隊作為權力最集中的機構之一，其性別平等進展可影響更廣的社會規範。","軍隊長期以男性為主導，女性常面臨晉升受限、性騷擾與制度排斥。提升效能需結構性改革，而不只是增加女性人數，還要改變評價體系和日常文化。","如果連最保守的軍隊都開始談性別平等，說明其他行業的藉口更站不住腳。軍隊中的變化可能產生示範效應，讓更多機構重新審視自己的性別盲區。"],"why":"在強調紀律和服從的軍隊裡討論女性晉升和效能，本身就是對舊結構的挑戰。","en":{"t":"Improving women's effectiveness in the military to advance gender equality","d":"Calls to enhance women's roles and effectiveness in military settings aim to promote gender equality.","body":["A report highlights efforts to improve women's effectiveness and equality in the military. It discusses structural barriers to advancement.","As a male-dominated institution, the military requires targeted reforms to address discrimination and promote women's progress."]},"img":"assets/img/workplace.png","src":"Vietnam.vn","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxQWGd0ODMxOVdLTmwzQVJaQzJpZFNNeG1uQWFLbGZmSEhMWDRRTmhhM2ZFVng3aVVkLWdvRUVQM1NrNW9yVWt4NHhZRnUzR1dUZk1MSDZ1R0EyYWpDMVNRVjExTW4xSHQ2ME15eXlPRFZYb1M1RnF2bWdGUnhJN0FTUkVzcjJOZ2p0NXVTaktGMmZNLWlUTG8wcnFlZTVDRHBsV3RxVzBsS3JHTU1YaG1Z?oc=5","region":"東南亞"}]}]},{"id":"002","date":"2026-09-18","period":"2026.09.14 – 2026.09.20","title":"性別平等倒計時與女性行動","summary":"聯合國警告性別平等仍需171年，韓國擬批准墮胎藥，美國得州與南非案件凸顯女性健康與安全危機；埃及、法國、巴西等地從職場、世俗性與地方治理推進權利討論。","en":{"title":"Gender Equality Countdown and Women's Actions","summary":"UN warns gender parity is still 171 years away, South Korea plans to approve abortion pills, cases in Texas and South Africa expose health and safety crises; Egypt, France and Brazil advance rights debates."},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","watch":{"name":"Michèle Vianès","name_en":"Michèle Vianès","role":"女性權利與世俗主義評論者","role_en":"Commentator on women's rights and secularism","region":"歐洲","why":"她在里昂媒體訪談中提出，世俗性是女性自主的必要條件而非充分條件，將宗教約束與制度支持放在同一分析框架裡，為法國爭論提供更平衡的視角。","why_en":"She argued that secularism is necessary but not sufficient for women's autonomy, linking religious constraints with institutional support.","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","img":""},"picks":{"film":"出走的決心","book":"第二性","art":"弗裡達·卡羅"},"sections":[{"cat":"國際","en_cat":"International","items":[{"id":"002-1","t":"聯合國警告：性別平等仍須171年","d":"聯合國新報告警告，女性權力正被削減，按當前速度實現全面性別平等還需171年，多個領域出現倒退。","body":["聯合國最新報告警示，女性在領導職位與公共領域的權力正在被削減，按當前速度實現全面性別平等還需171年。報告指出多個國家女性政治和經濟參與度下降，制度性承諾出現倒退。","報告將倒退歸因於部分國家削弱婦女權利機構、反性別議程抬頭以及氣候與衝突危機中對女性的忽視。過去幾年女性在議會、企業高管和司法系統的比例增長緩慢，某些地區甚至回落。","這一倒計時並非抽象數字；它意味著出生在今天的女孩在其有生之年仍可能面對法律、薪資與安全的不平等。報告呼籲把女性權利納入財政與社會政策核心，而非作為邊緣議題。"],"why":"171年的推算把遙遠的不平等變成一個可感知的時間長度，暴露承諾與行動的巨大落差。","en":{"t":"UN: Gender Equality Still 171 Years Away","d":"A new UN report warns women's power is being cut back, and at current pace full gender parity will take 171 years.","body":["The UN says women's power in leadership and public life is being cut back, with full gender equality 171 years away at the current pace. Several countries saw declines in women's political and economic participation.","The report blames weakened women's rights institutions, rising anti-gender agendas, and the neglect of women in climate and conflict crises. It calls for women's rights to be central to fiscal and social policy."]},"img":"assets/img/podium.png?v=3","src":"Devdiscourse","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","region":"全球"}]},{"cat":"生育權利","en_cat":"Reproductive Rights","items":[{"id":"002-2","t":"韓國擬明年批准墮胎藥","d":"韓國計劃明年批准藥物墮胎，結束多年僅允許手術墮胎的限制，改善女性終止妊娠的可及性與隱私。","body":["韓國政府計劃在明年批准墮胎藥的使用。此前藥物墮胎在韓國長期未獲正式許可，有需要的女性多依賴手術或其他路徑，在時間與費用上承受額外負擔。","韓國憲法法院此前已裁定將墮胎全面入罪違憲，但配套立法與藥品審批推進緩慢。醫學上，藥物終止妊娠常用於孕早期，侵入性較低且隱私性更高，但其合法化需要配套的處方與隨訪制度。","若獲批，韓國女性將多一種不必進入手術室的選擇，這在醫療資源集中在都市的地區尤其重要。爭議在於藥品上市後的費用是否納入醫保，以及偏遠地區能否獲得規範用藥指導。"],"why":"韓國墮胎早已非罪，藥物墮胎卻拖到明年才可能獲批，法律與醫療選項長期脫節。","en":{"t":"South Korea Expected to Approve Abortion Pills Next Year","d":"Seoul plans to approve medication abortion, expanding options beyond surgery after years of delay.","body":["South Korea plans to approve abortion pills next year, giving women a non-surgical option after long delays. The move follows a court ruling that criminalizing abortion was unconstitutional.","Medication abortion is used for early pregnancy and offers more privacy, but approval requires prescription and follow-up systems. Cost coverage and access outside major cities remain contentious."]},"img":"assets/img/body-choice.png?v=3","src":"yahoo.com","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPbmw2cVFack9UMnBpcXFwaU9jMzYyTkttZV9ya3MxR3VEdHlGcmJsYVdyUmN6OElqLUpUckdYM0tCNUpKLURvd1hnN2ZSMFJKUTNZMW9yX1ByRWtqRFkyRWxid2xlR0I0aE9rYm5lQVJNNXhyNGdnQ0o2bVlYY0ZZRGNSSHFSODZ6OG8xVnhIWFpTaFE?oc=5","region":"東亞"}]},{"cat":"健康與權益","en_cat":"Health & Rights","items":[{"id":"002-3","t":"訴訟：得州墮胎禁令導致孕婦死亡","d":"美國得州一名孕婦據稱因墮胎禁令延誤救治而死亡，其家屬提起訴訟，再度引發對孕產健康與限制性法律衝突的關注。","body":["一項在美國得州提起的訴訟稱，該州墮胎禁令導致一名孕婦死亡。原告主張醫療人員因法律風險未能及時提供終止妊娠處理，延誤了必要治療，最終造成悲劇。","得州實施嚴格的墮胎限制，許多醫生在高額罰則與刑事風險下，即使面對健康受威脅的孕婦也趨於保守，孕產急救面臨不確定性。","這類案件將抽象的墮胎法律轉化為可驗證的醫療後果，可能影響後續司法審查與立法辯論。它也促使公眾關注：在限制墮胎的州，妊娠併發症和產科急症是否得到同等保護。"],"why":"死亡訴訟把墮胎爭論從道德立場拉回到醫療現實，法律可能正在產生直接傷害。","en":{"t":"Lawsuit: Texas Abortion Ban Caused Pregnant Woman's Death","d":"A lawsuit in Texas claims the state's abortion ban led to a pregnant woman's death by delaying necessary care.","body":["The suit says medical providers feared legal consequences and failed to provide timely termination, leading to the woman's death. Texas has strict abortion limits with high penalties.","The case turns abstract abortion law into measurable health outcomes and may influence judicial review. It raises questions about equal protection for pregnancy complications in restrictive states."]},"img":"assets/img/body-choice.png?v=3","src":"NBC News","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQUTYxZUUxVi1hZmFZQVRKYllTNGdyOXMwNmJfa3VyRTlkNTVGTHhxS2dpNGJBa0dhcmpJQkZ2dVlYZ0FJRE9QLUFQV0Z1d05BR1J1Tlh3OExQZXRnd01MSmR4Yms3Q2YwdzlCc1hSOXFkQTlaMFg2WDhkUTZXR3E2RUZLcWxpLThrSFgtckdNdXdXNHRESTFRMWxLYUFsQ3hDeGpETlNORklsdEtOd0FyekVvSndDZw?oc=5","region":"北美"}]},{"cat":"社會","en_cat":"Society","items":[{"id":"002-4","t":"南非系列殺害女性案發現第九具遺體","d":"南非調查針對女性的連環殺害案時，發現第九具女性遺體，性別暴力問題再度成為全國焦點。","body":["南非警方在調查一系列以女性為目標的殺害案件時，發現第九具女性遺體。屍體被發現地點與先前案件存在關聯，警方尚未確認是否同一兇手，但已成立專案組。","南非長期面臨高發的基於性別的暴力與殺害。犯罪率高企、執法資源不足和貧困使女性處於風險之中，家暴與陌生人暴力交織，許多案件未能及時偵破。","連續發現遺體暴露出女性人身安全的系統性危機，民間組織呼籲將性別暴力視為國家緊急狀態。案件也促使公眾質疑警方在早期是否忽視失蹤報案與社區線索。"],"why":"九具遺體並非孤立兇案，而是同一地區女性不斷遇害的連續信號。","en":{"t":"Ninth Body Found in South Africa Serial Killings of Women","d":"South African police found a ninth body while probing a series of killings targeting women, intensifying focus on gender-based violence.","body":["The body was found in an area linked to previous cases, and police have formed a task team. South Africa faces high rates of gender-based violence, with many cases unsolved.","The deaths expose a systemic crisis in women's safety, and activists demand that gender violence be treated as a national emergency. Questions are raised about early police response to missing women."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png?v=3","src":"Al Jazeera","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","region":"非洲"},{"id":"002-5","t":"法國評論：世俗性是女性自主的必要條件而非充分條件","d":"里昂媒體刊出Michèle Vianès訪談，認為世俗性保護女性免受宗教約束，但不是女性自主的充分條件，還需制度與教育支持。","body":["法國評論者Michèle Vianès在里昂媒體訪談中表示，世俗性本身不足以讓女性成為自主個體，但它是不可或缺的條件。她認為剝離宗教對公共生活的控制，為女性獨立選擇創造了空間。","在法國，圍繞穆斯林頭巾、性別平等與共和價值觀的爭論持續多年。世俗主義常被不同陣營用作工具，或強調個體自由，或強調公共秩序，女性權益處於交叉地帶。","該觀點提出一個平衡點：反對宗教對女性的強制，但也要警惕用世俗主義壓制文化身份或忽視經濟結構。女性自主需要教育、就業和反歧視法律的共同支撐。"],"why":"把世俗性定位為條件而非答案，跳出了宗教自由與女性權利非此即彼的簡單對立。","en":{"t":"French Commentator: Secularism Is Necessary but Not Sufficient for Women's Autonomy","d":"Michèle Vianès argues in Lyon Capitale that secularism is an indispensable condition but not a complete answer for women's autonomy.","body":["She says removing religion from public life creates space for women's independent choices. In France, debates over headscarves and republican values often use secularism as a political tool.","Her position balances opposition to religious coercion with concern about using secularism to suppress cultural identity. Autonomy requires education, employment and anti-discrimination law."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png?v=3","src":"Lyon Capitale","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","region":"歐洲"},{"id":"002-6","t":"澳大利亞性別平等排名創史上最高","d":"澳大利亞在最新性別平等排名中取得有史以來最好成績，男女在教育、就業與政治領域的差距縮小，但仍未完全消除。","body":["澳大利亞在最新發布的性別平等排名中，男女平等程度創下有記錄以來最高。報道顯示，該國在教育程度、勞動參與和政治代表性上的性別差距有所縮小。","澳大利亞在女性教育水平上長期領先，但職場隔離、無償照料負擔和薪資差距仍存在。排名提升更多反映部分領域改善，而非結構性障礙的全面消除。","排名可作為政策參考，但也可能掩蓋邊緣群體中差距擴大的現實。移民、原住民和低收入女性的處境未必與平均值同步改善，需要更細化的數據評估。"],"why":"排名提升容易製造樂觀，但平均值會掩蓋特定女性群體的停滯甚至倒退。","en":{"t":"Australia Records Best-Ever Gender Equality Ranking","d":"Australia achieved its highest gender equality ranking, but structural gaps in work and care remain hidden by averages.","body":["Improvements in education, participation and political representation drove the ranking, but job segregation and pay gaps persist.","The average may mask widening inequality for migrants, Indigenous and low-income women, requiring more granular data."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png?v=3","src":"Yahoo News Australia","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiekFVX3lxTE5sRnp6UHV3R2FISnRQbklMWTVOOG9RZTZJeDlkaFA0UEQxdWhocFVwUGVscGhRWDZ2Q3VmNkhjbWhoelJoTkwyS0FNYThnV2xteXBQWDBVUnJ6RkwzUm45Z0RobHFKUldyWjhuOEthQmo4OWlQUmdIWU93?oc=5","region":"大洋洲"}]},{"cat":"職場平等","en_cat":"Workplace Equality","items":[{"id":"002-7","t":"埃及媒體討論女性薪酬權與決策參與","d":"埃及官方媒體刊文討論女性獲得同等報酬與參與決策的權利，呼籲在經濟與治理中推動性別平等。","body":["埃及國家媒體發表文章，討論女性在職場獲得同等報酬和參與決策的權利。文章指出，女性經濟參與雖有進展，但薪資差距和決策層中的缺席仍限制其影響力。","中東多國女性勞動參與率低於全球水平，文化規範和育兒責任常將女性擠出正式就業。決策結構中的男性主導使涉及女性利益的政策難以被優先考慮。","文章將薪酬與決策權聯繫起來，強調經濟賦權不僅關乎個人收入，也改變家庭和社會中的權力分配。實現這些權利需要法律執行與企業治理的持續壓力。"],"why":"官方媒體主動討論薪酬與決策權，說明該議題已進入體制話語，但仍停留在呼籲層面。","en":{"t":"Egyptian Media Discuss Women's Right to Equal Pay and Decision-Making","d":"Egypt's state media published an article on women's equal pay and participation in decision-making, urging progress in the economy and governance.","body":["The article notes that despite women's economic advancement, wage gaps and absence from decision-making limit their influence. Cultural norms and care responsibilities push women out of formal employment.","Linking pay with decision-making shows economic empowerment changes power in family and society. Progress requires legal enforcement and corporate governance pressure."]},"img":"assets/img/workplace.png?v=3","src":"الهيئة الوطنية للإعلام","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","region":"中東"}]},{"cat":"政策與法律","en_cat":"Policy & Law","items":[{"id":"002-8","t":"巴西馬利利亞擴大婦女權利委員會社會參與","d":"巴西馬利利亞市擴大婦女權利委員會的社會參與，加強民間組織在政策制定中的角色，提升性別議題地方治理代表性。","body":["巴西馬利利亞市政府宣佈擴大婦女權利委員會的社會參與，吸納更多民間組織與女性代表進入諮詢與決策過程。該舉措旨在讓地方性別政策更貼近實際需求。","巴西在婦女權利和反家暴領域有較高法律標準，但政策執行常受地方財政與保守勢力影響。市政委員會是連接法律與社區的重要機制，此前常因代表性不足而功能有限。","擴大參與有利於將分散的婦女服務與訴求納入制度化渠道，但真正的挑戰在於委員會建議能否轉化為預算與行動。地方治理的透明度與執行承諾決定其成效。"],"why":"婦女委員會擴權看似程序性調整，實則改變誰能在地方政策中發聲的權力分佈。","en":{"t":"Marília Expands Social Participation in Women's Rights Council","d":"The Brazilian city of Marília expanded social participation in its Municipal Council for Women's Rights, strengthening civil society's role in policy.","body":["The move brings more civil organizations and women representatives into consultation and decision-making, aiming to align local gender policy with needs.","The challenge is translating council recommendations into budget and action. Local transparency and enforcement will determine whether participation leads to real change."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","src":"conexaomarilia.com.br","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxNTEpIdU9hRFkyeTlITkczWXIzNEFwbXo0eWsxZ0taUEJNSV83cmZ6ekxWQ2Z5TElOZnNlTGFoWWgzMUJSbm85UWJqOFBDS1lLLV9CUFNydjZQWHd5aTBvcEREMHp3ZTJWbjd0dnZlc0NGaEI5d0FXd3lnWjl1LTc3ZnI1U2hDUVpHSGthRWUxOV9ldTNkWWcybXMtNWZ0WHhSdnRBdGkxYVZobUlUdHdwSHZSVEhuaTRROXd3aVQyckcwd2Z4?oc=5","region":"拉美"},{"id":"002-9","t":"斯里蘭卡評論：女性權利關乎實質平等","d":"斯里蘭卡媒體刊文指出，女性權利的核心是實質平等而非僅形式平等，需消除結果上的差距和結構性障礙。","body":["斯里蘭卡媒體評論指出，女性權利不能停留在法律條文的形式平等，而應追求實質平等。作者強調，即使法律禁止歧視，資源和機會分配上的差距仍使女性處於不利地位。","南亞多國在憲法與勞動法中都有平等條款，但土地繼承、非正式就業和家庭照料的不平等使女性難以實現經濟獨立。性別配額等政策往往面臨實施軟化和地方阻力。","實質平等的概念要求正視歷史累積的不利，並在就業、教育、社會保障等方面採取積極措施。這對政策制定者提出更高標準，也引發關於特殊措施是否造成反向歧視的爭論。"],"why":"把焦點從權利義務拉向結果差距，暴露了紙面平等與實際生活之間的脫節。","en":{"t":"Sri Lankan Commentary: Women's Rights Are About Substantive Equality","d":"A Sri Lankan article argues that women's rights require substantive equality, not just formal legal provisions, to close outcome gaps.","body":["Even where discrimination is banned, gaps in resources and opportunity keep women disadvantaged. South Asian legal equality often fails against unequal land, informal work and care burdens.","Substantive equality demands positive measures in employment, education and social protection, but also raises debate about reverse discrimination."]},"img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","src":"themorning.lk","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZkFVX3lxTE1xRk12UURFUzFyVW1PTHJLanlRQ0FNWXhjcVJQaXFQcDZLa3BKN1B5UHVtXzNTc0pZV3JNN2U4aUZhTWd4MFNOaWk3ZGV5dERyZkdTem9pY2g1cTRfMzVremxHdjVMZw?oc=5","region":"南亞"}]},{"cat":"體育","en_cat":"Sports","items":[{"id":"002-10","t":"菲律賓女籃亞運會首戰力克哈薩克斯坦","d":"菲律賓Gilas女籃在亞運會首場比賽中大勝哈薩克斯坦，為賽事取得開門紅，團隊表現亮眼。","body":["菲律賓Gilas女籃在亞運會首場比賽中擊敗哈薩克斯坦隊，以強勢表現開啟賽事征程。球隊在攻防兩端佔據主動，為晉級目標奠定基礎。","東南亞女子籃球長期缺乏曝光與資源，菲律賓近年通過海外訓練和聯賽改革提升競爭力。國家隊成績被視為推動女性參與體育和爭取職業機會的重要窗口。","女子比賽的成績能吸引更多年輕女性投身運動，但獎牌之外，薪酬、轉播和贊助的不平等仍是區域女籃面臨的共同困境。賽事曝光帶來的關注度能否轉化為長期投入仍需觀察。"],"why":"女籃國家隊大勝不易，但這類消息通常只在綜合運動會期間得到短暫關注。","en":{"t":"Philippines' Gilas Women Dominate Kazakhstan in Asian Games Opener","d":"The Philippine women's basketball team beat Kazakhstan in its first Asian Games match, starting the campaign strongly.","body":["The team controlled both ends and set a foundation for advancing. Southeast Asian women's basketball has lacked exposure and resources, with recent reforms boosting competitiveness.","Sustained funding and media visibility remain challenges beyond medals. The performance may inspire young women but needs institutional support to translate into long-term change."]},"img":"assets/img/women-power.png?v=3","src":"ABS-CBN","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxNb1NuTFpPN2NwaWVpTWZKaXhHcjJ0aFdKbFc0enpmMk13T0hvUXN3aEhfMlBMSk9mNV96Z2lvU2VYTzJsVk00R0tvOVM0Q2RQUHVOOHB6NzFVM3JyWWtrWkllQ3ZZaHlYUkltN2RWQThSSGU0bHhCSHlHOGVFRlpaakdqYk5ERmFub0x4LVQ2eXlPdkNoYTNhR1IxN0M2WXRUVF9kbkp0VGxCY2wwVE9hVFJCTFd1dTJ6aDlWVjB2clNfYzQ?oc=5","region":"東南亞"}]}]},{"id":"001","img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","date":"2026-09-17","period":"2026.09.14 – 2026.09.20","title":"她照亮歷史：金獅、法案與“120年”之問","en":{"title":"She Lights Up History: A Golden Lion, a New Law, and the 120-Year Question","summary":"This week's global roundup: May el-Toukhy wins Venice's Golden Lion, France moves to tighten sexual-violence laws, the WEF warns gender parity is still 120 years away, and Mexico's abortion win inspires the US."},"summary":"本期覆蓋全球、歐洲、北美、拉美、中東、非洲、東亞、南亞、大洋洲與中國：梅爾·圖琪摘金獅，法國推進打擊性暴力法案，世經論壇警告全球性別平等還需120年，墨西哥墮胎權勝利啟示美國，日本性別平等排名繼續G7墊底。","sections":[{"cat":"國際","en_cat":"International","items":[{"id":"001-1","img":"assets/img/vote.png?v=3","t":"世界經濟論壇：全球性別平等還需120年","d":"世界經濟論壇最新報告警告：按當前速度，全球性別平等仍需要約120年才能實現，呼籲各國加快縮小差距。","en":{"t":"WEF: Global Gender Parity Is Still 120 Years Away","d":"The World Economic Forum's latest report warns that at the current pace, full global gender parity will take about 120 years — and urges governments and business to accelerate.","body":["\"Gender parity is still 120 years away.\" That is the sobering headline of the World Economic Forum's latest Global Gender Gap Report, which tracks gaps in economic participation, education, health and political empowerment.","The widest gap remains in economic participation: unequal pay, the leadership ceiling and the unequal distribution of unpaid care work continue to slow women's advancement. Education gaps have largely closed — yet that progress has not automatically translated into equality at work and in decision-making.","The report urges governments and companies to treat gender equality as a core agenda, not a side topic: expanding paid parental leave, raising women's representation on boards and in parliaments, and investing in women's health and digital skills."]},"body":["“全球性別平等還需120年。”這是世界經濟論壇最新一期全球性別差距報告給出的判斷。報告追蹤經濟參與、教育、健康與政治賦權四大維度，指出全球性別差距雖在緩慢收窄，但速度遠不足以讓這一代人看到終點。","報告特別指出，經濟參與與機會是差距最大的領域之一：同工不同酬、職業天花板與照護勞動的不平等分配，仍在系統性拖慢女性進入關鍵崗位的速度。教育維度的差距已基本彌合，但並未自動轉化為職場與決策層的平等。","報告呼籲各國政府與企業將性別平等納入核心議程，而不僅是“附加議題”：擴大帶薪育兒假、提高女性在董事會與政壇的比例、投資女性健康與數字技能，都被列為加速路徑。"],"src":"TRT中文","url":"https://www.trtzhongwen.com/article/1e667f50d109","region":"全球"},{"id":"001-2","img":"assets/img/podium.png?v=3","t":"聯合國婦女署出席第81屆聯合國大會","d":"聯合國婦女署在聯大期間發聲：性別平等議程“從未如此相關”，呼籲以國家領導力與持續夥伴關係推進婦女議題。","en":{"t":"UN Women at the 81st UN General Assembly","d":"At this year's General Assembly, UN Women declares that the gender-equality mandate has \"never been more relevant\", calling for national leadership and sustained partnership.","body":["As the 81st session of the UN General Assembly convenes, UN Women has issued a clear message: the gender-equality mandate is more urgent than ever. From women and girls in conflict zones to women workers hit hardest by economic crises, the cost of inequality is increasingly visible.","\"You gave us a mandate that has never been more relevant,\" UN Women said, urging member states to back commitments with national leadership, institutions and sustained funding — especially as progress on Sustainable Development Goal 5 lags.","During the Assembly, UN Women will hold side events and high-level dialogues on women's economic empowerment, ending violence against women, and women's participation in peace and security."]},"body":["在第81屆聯合國大會召開之際，聯合國婦女署發佈媒體公告與講話，重申性別平等在全球議程中的優先地位。婦女署指出，從衝突地區的婦女與女童，到經濟危機中首當其衝的女性勞動者，性別不平等的代價正在被越來越清晰地看見。","婦女署強調，“你們賦予我們的使命從未如此相關”。在實現2030可持續發展目標（尤其是目標5：性別平等）的進程明顯滯後的背景下，婦女署呼籲成員國拿出國家層面的領導力，並以制度與資金的雙重投入兌現承諾。","本屆聯大期間，婦女署將圍繞婦女經濟賦權、結束針對婦女的暴力、以及婦女在和平與安全中的參與等議題開展系列邊會與高級別對話。"],"src":"UN Women","url":"https://www.unwomen.org/en/news-stories/media-advisory/2026/09/un-women-at-the-81st-session-of-the-un-general-assembly-unga-81","region":"全球"},{"id":"001-3","img":"assets/img/workplace.png?v=3","t":"利比里亞：300萬美元倡議推動女性領導力與和平建設","d":"聯合國婦女署與合作伙伴啟動300萬美元倡議，支持利比里亞女性在領導力、司法與和平建設中的參與。","en":{"t":"Liberia: US$3 Million Initiative to Advance Women's Leadership and Peacebuilding","d":"UN Women and partners roll out a US$3 million initiative to strengthen Liberian women's participation in leadership, justice and peacebuilding.","body":["UN Women and partners have launched a US$3 million initiative in Liberia focused on three pillars: women's leadership, justice and peacebuilding. Liberia made history in 2006 by electing Africa's first female head of state, yet women's share of decision-making has not kept growing in the post-war years.","The initiative will build the capacity of grassroots women's organisations, support women candidates in local governance, and improve the justice system's response to gender-based violence. In peacebuilding, women's voices will be woven into community mediation and national dialogue mechanisms.","As UN Women's regional office puts it, in post-conflict countries every additional seat for women in peace processes makes agreements more durable — so this investment is aimed squarely at sustainable peace."]},"body":["聯合國婦女署與合作伙伴宣佈，在利比里亞啟動一項總額300萬美元的新倡議，聚焦三個方向：女性領導力、司法正義與和平建設。利比里亞曾在2006年選出非洲首位民選女總統，但戰後的重建進程並未讓女性在決策層的佔比持續擴大。","倡議將支持基層女性組織的能力建設，幫助女性候選人參與地方治理，並推動司法系統對性別暴力案件的回應。和平建設部分則將女性的聲音納入社區衝突調解與國家對話機制。","婦女署非洲區域辦公室表示，在衝突後國家，女性參與和平進程每增加一分，和平協議的可持續性就提高一分——這筆投資因此被看作對“可持續和平”的直接投入。"],"src":"UN Women Africa","url":"https://africa.unwomen.org/en/stories/news/2026/09/un-women-and-partners-roll-out-us3-million-initiative-to-advance-womens-leadership-justice-and-peacebuilding-in-liberia","region":"非洲"}]},{"cat":"政策與法律","en_cat":"Policy & Law","items":[{"id":"001-4","img":"assets/img/women-power.png?v=3","t":"法國：受“莉安娜案”推動，打擊性暴力法案10月審議","d":"在社會輿論推動下，法國打擊性暴力法案將於10月進入審議，強化對性暴力犯罪的追訴與受害者保護。","en":{"t":"France: Sexual-Violence Bill to Be Reviewed in October, Driven by the 'Liana Case'","d":"Spurred by a high-profile case and public pressure, a French bill strengthening prosecution of sexual violence and victim protection heads to parliamentary review in October.","body":["According to Oushinet (European Times), a French bill toughening the fight against sexual violence will enter parliamentary review in October. Its acceleration is widely linked to the nationwide outcry over the \"Liana case\", which cast doubt on how the justice system handles sexual-violence complaints.","The bill aims to lower evidentiary and prosecution thresholds, extend limitation periods for certain offences, and strengthen procedural protection and support for victims. Advocates argue France's current consent standards and procedures place an unreasonable burden on survivors.","After years of back-and-forth over consent age and the legal definition of sexual violence, this bill — if passed — would rank among the most significant French legislative steps of the post-#MeToo era."]},"body":["據歐洲時報報道，法國一項旨在加強打擊性暴力的法案將於10月進入議會審議。輿論普遍認為，該法案的加速推進與近期引發全國關注的“莉安娜案”直接相關——這起案件讓公眾對司法系統處理性暴力案件的方式提出強烈質疑。","法案的核心方向包括：降低性暴力案件的舉證與追訴門檻、延長部分罪行的追訴時效，以及強化對受害者的程序保護與援助。支持者認為，法國現行的“同意”認定標準與辦案流程對受害者過於苛刻。","過去幾年，法國圍繞“同意年齡”與性暴力定義的立法討論反覆拉鋸。此次法案若獲通過，將成為該國#MeToo時代以來最重要的性暴力立法進展之一。"],"src":"歐洲時報","url":"https://www.oushinet.com/static/content/france/2026-09-02/1544740884166357230.html","region":"歐洲"},{"id":"001-5","img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","t":"《浙江省婦女權益保障條例》正式落地","d":"條例施行後，浙江多地啟動普法基層行活動，推動婦女權益保障從紙面走向實踐。","en":{"t":"Zhejiang's Regulation on Women's Rights Protection Takes Effect","d":"With the new regulation in force, Zhejiang launches grassroots legal-awareness campaigns to turn women's rights protection from paper into practice.","body":["Zhejiang Province's Regulation on the Protection of Women's Rights and Interests took effect this month, adding local detail to the national law — covering employment, marriage and family, personal safety and property rights, and spelling out the responsibilities of employers, grassroots organisations and government departments.","To support implementation, Zhejiang has launched community-level legal-awareness campaigns — talks, case exhibitions and free legal clinics that translate legal language into everyday terms. A second round is already underway in districts such as Xiaoshan in Hangzhou.","The rollout is seen as part of a chain from national legislation through local regulation to grassroots enforcement — because the life of a law, ultimately, lies in its implementation."]},"body":["《浙江省婦女權益保障條例》本月正式施行，成為繼國家上位法修訂後，地方層面配套落地的又一重要法規。條例細化了婦女在就業、婚姻家庭、人身安全與財產權益等方面的保護條款，並明確了用人單位、基層組織與政府部門的責任分工。","為配合條例落地，浙江多地啟動“普法基層行”活動，通過社區宣講、案例展板與法律諮詢，把條款翻譯成普通家庭聽得懂的語言。活動第二期已在杭州蕭山等區縣展開。","地方條例的密集出臺，被視為中國婦女權益保障“國家立法—地方配套—基層執行”鏈條補全的信號：法律的生命，正在於落地。"],"src":"澎湃新聞","url":"https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_34031959","region":"中國"},{"id":"001-6","img":"assets/img/body-choice.png?v=3","t":"美國：聯邦上訴法院再次審理米非司酮案","d":"針對墮胎藥物米非司酮的訴訟再度進入聯邦上訴法院，ACLU呼籲駁回“毫無根據”的挑戰。","en":{"t":"US: Federal Appeals Court Hears Mifepristone Challenge — Again","d":"The long-running lawsuit against the abortion pill mifepristone returns to a federal appeals court, with the ACLU urging judges to reject a \"baseless\" challenge.","body":["The legal battle over mifepristone has returned to a federal appeals court. Since the Supreme Court dismissed standing in 2024, anti-abortion groups have mounted a fresh challenge targeting the FDA's decades-old approval and regulation of the drug.","The ACLU calls the case \"baseless\", citing decades of research on the drug's safety, and warns that restricting mifepristone would deal a heavy blow to medication abortion nationwide — especially in states where clinic access has already collapsed.","Medication abortion now accounts for more than 60% of abortions in the United States. The case is being watched as a key test of reproductive rights in the post-Roe era."]},"body":["圍繞墮胎藥物米非司酮的訴訟再次來到聯邦上訴法院。這是自美國最高法院2024年駁回原告資格以來，反對墮胎團體對米非司酮發起的又一輪法律挑戰，目標直指FDA對該藥物二十餘年的批准與使用規則。","美國公民自由聯盟（ACLU）在聲明中稱這場挑戰“毫無根據”，指出米非司酮的安全性已被數十項研究證實，並警告：若限制令成立，全美藥物流產的可及性將受到嚴重衝擊，尤其是在墮胎服務已大幅收縮的州。","藥物流產如今佔美國人工終止妊娠總數的六成以上。此案的走向，被視為羅訴韋德案被推翻後，美國生育權利博弈的又一個關鍵觀察點。"],"src":"ACLU","url":"https://www.aclu.org/press-releases/federal-appeals-court-hears-baseless-challenge-to-the-abortion-pill-mifepristone-again","region":"北美"}]},{"cat":"健康與權益","en_cat":"Health & Rights","items":[{"id":"001-7","img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","t":"美國：宮外孕死亡人數近翻倍，得州尤甚","d":"研究顯示美國宮外孕死亡人數幾乎翻倍，限制墮胎的州情況更為嚴峻，引發對孕產婦健康的廣泛擔憂。","en":{"t":"US: Ectopic Pregnancy Deaths Have Nearly Doubled — and It's Worse in Texas","d":"New research shows ectopic-pregnancy deaths in the US have nearly doubled, with the sharpest toll in abortion-restrictive states like Texas.","body":["New research cited by the National Partnership for Women & Families shows that ectopic-pregnancy deaths in the United States have nearly doubled in recent years — with the worst outcomes in states with the strictest abortion bans, such as Texas. An ectopic pregnancy is never viable and can be fatal without prompt treatment.","Researchers point to delays in care: in states with bans, doctors fearing legal liability may postpone treatment of emergencies like ectopic pregnancy until a patient's life is visibly at risk — turning preventable tragedies into reality.","The report calls on states to enact clear emergency exceptions and liability shields so clinicians can save lives without fear of prosecution. Maternal health has become the heaviest footnote in America's abortion debate."]},"body":["美國國家婦女與家庭夥伴關係組織援引的最新研究顯示，美國宮外孕死亡人數在近年幾乎翻倍，而在墮胎限制最嚴格的得克薩斯州，情況更為嚴峻。宮外孕無法繼續妊娠且若不及時處理可危及生命，醫療處置的延誤是關鍵風險因素。","研究者指出，在墮胎禁令生效的州，醫生出於對法律風險的顧慮，可能推遲對宮外孕等急症的處理，直到患者出現生命危險。這種“延誤醫療”正在把本可避免的悲劇變成現實。","報告呼籲各州立法明確急診例外條款，並建立醫療機構的免責機制，讓醫生能夠“依法救人而不必懼怕訴訟”。孕產婦健康正在成為美國生育權利爭論中最沉重的註腳。"],"src":"National Partnership for Women & Families","url":"https://nationalpartnership.org/news-ectopic-pregnancy-deaths-have-nearly-doubled-and-its-worse-in-texas/","region":"北美"}]},{"cat":"職場平等","en_cat":"Workplace Equality","items":[{"id":"001-8","img":"assets/img/workplace.png?v=3","t":"日本：性別平等排名全球第117位，繼續G7墊底","d":"最新排名顯示日本男女平等指數僅列全球第117位，在七國集團中持續墊底，職場與政界的性別差距仍是焦點。","en":{"t":"Japan Ranks 117th in Global Gender Equality — Still Last in the G7","d":"The latest index places Japan 117th worldwide for gender equality, again the worst among G7 nations, with workplace and political gaps in the spotlight.","body":["According to Japan's Overseas Chinese News, Japan ranks 117th in the latest Global Gender Gap Index — once again last among the G7. The World Economic Forum index shows Japan scoring persistently low on political empowerment and women in management.","Women's share of parliamentary seats and of corporate boards remains far below major Western economies. Although the government targets 30% of leadership roles for women by 2030, critics say the goal lacks enforcement and adequate childcare support.","Ageing and labour shortages should have made women's participation an economic necessity — but the high share of women in non-regular work and stubborn pay gaps keep the promise of \"womenomics\" unfulfilled."]},"body":["據日本華僑報報道，在最新一期全球性別差距指數中，日本位列第117位，繼續在七國集團中墊底。這份由世界經濟論壇編制的指數顯示，日本在政治賦權與企業管理層女性比例上的得分長期徘徊在低位。","日本國會中女性議員的佔比、上市公司女性董事的比例，均遠低於歐美主要經濟體。儘管政府提出“到2030年將女性管理層比例提升至30%”的目標，但批評者指出，缺乏強制力與配套育兒支持的目標更像口號。","人口老齡化與勞動力短缺本應成為推動女性就業的契機，但非正規僱傭中女性佔比偏高、同工不同酬等問題，讓“女性經濟學”始終未能兌現其承諾。"],"src":"日本華僑報","url":"http://www.jnocnews.co.jp/n161407.html","region":"東亞"},{"id":"001-9","img":"assets/img/workplace.png?v=3","t":"澳大利亞：男女平等排名創歷史新高","d":"最新數據顯示澳大利亞男女平等程度達到有記錄以來的最高水平。","en":{"t":"Australia: Gender Equality Ranking Hits Record High","d":"New data shows Australian men and women are more equal than ever on record.","body":["New data shows gender equality in Australia has reached its highest level on record, driven by steady gains in women's employment, leadership representation and educational attainment.","Analysts credit a mix of policies: mandatory publication of gender pay gaps, childcare subsidy reform, and the spread of corporate diversity targets. Yet occupational segregation in sectors such as mining and construction remains visible.","At a time when progress is stalling in many developed economies, Australia's upward curve is being studied as evidence that a well-designed policy mix can work."]},"body":["澳大利亞最新數據顯示，該國男女平等程度達到有記錄以來的最高水平。這一進展體現在女性就業率、管理層比例與教育獲得的持續改善上。","分析人士指出，強制性的性別薪酬差距公示制度、育兒補貼改革與企業多元目標的普及，是推動排名的關鍵政策組合。不過，礦業與建築等傳統行業的性別隔離依然明顯。","在多數發達國家性別平等進展趨緩的背景下，澳大利亞的上升曲線被研究者視為“政策組合拳”可以奏效的例證。"],"src":"AAP","url":"https://www.dailymail.com/wires/aap/article-16135631/Aussie-men-women-ranking-equal-ever.html","region":"大洋洲"}]},{"cat":"生育權利","en_cat":"Reproductive Rights","items":[{"id":"001-10","img":"assets/img/women-power.png?v=3","t":"墨西哥的墮胎權勝利：拉美經驗或為美國提供借鑑","d":"拉美女性權利組織指出，墨西哥在墮胎去罪化上的勝利，或為正在激烈博弈的美國提供經驗與路徑。","en":{"t":"Mexico's Abortion Victory: Latin America's Lessons for the US","d":"Latin American women's rights groups say Mexico's decriminalisation win may hold the key to the US struggle.","body":["Latin American women's rights groups argue that Mexico's abortion decriminalisation could offer lessons for the United States. After Mexico's Supreme Court ruled criminalisation unconstitutional, state after state followed — part of the movement known as the \"Green Wave\".","The Green Wave's playbook: reframe abortion from a moral dispute to a question of public health and freedom, advance through both courts and streets, and build cross-class solidarity around simple symbols such as the green scarf. With Argentina and Colombia following suit, Latin America has become one of the world's most dynamic fronts for reproductive rights.","Activists caution that transplanting the playbook to America's federal system and polarised politics is hard — and that the region's own lesson applies equally: decriminalisation is not the same as access, and getting services to women in remote areas is the second half of the fight."]},"body":["拉美女性權利組織近期表示，墨西哥在墮胎去罪化上取得的勝利，或能為正在激烈博弈的美國提供經驗與路徑。過去數年，墨西哥最高法院裁定墮胎入刑違憲，各州相繼跟進，形成被稱為“綠色浪潮”的運動。","“綠色浪潮”的核心經驗在於：把墮胎權從道德爭議重構為公共衛生與自由議題，通過司法途徑與街頭運動雙線推進，並以圍巾等符號建立跨階層認同。阿根廷、哥倫比亞的相繼去罪化，讓拉美成為全球生育權利運動最活躍的地區之一。","活動人士坦言，美國的聯邦體制與兩黨極化使經驗移植並不簡單，但“去罪化不等於醫療可及”的教訓同樣深刻：法律勝利之後，如何讓偏遠地區的女性真正獲得服務，是拉美與美國共同的下半場。"],"src":"KRGV","url":"https://www.krgv.com/news/latin-america-women-s-rights-groups-say-their-abortion-win-in-mexico-may-hold-the-key-to-us-struggle","region":"拉美"}]},{"cat":"社會","en_cat":"Society","items":[{"id":"001-11","img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","t":"穆斯林世界聯盟：針對女性的暴力沒有伊斯蘭合法性","d":"穆斯林世界聯盟負責人公開表示，暴力侵害女性沒有任何伊斯蘭教法依據，呼籲穆斯林社會共同反對基於性別的暴力。","en":{"t":"Muslim World League: Violence Against Women Has No Islamic Legitimacy","d":"The head of the Muslim World League publicly states that violence against women has no basis in Islamic law, urging Muslim societies to reject gender-based violence.","body":["The Secretary-General of the Muslim World League has issued a public statement declaring that \"violence against women has no Islamic legitimacy\" — a line widely read as a formal boundary drawn by one of the Islamic world's most authoritative bodies.","The statement stresses that violence against women violates the foundational principles of Islamic law and contradicts a long tradition of honouring women's dignity and rights. It urges Muslim scholars, religious institutions and civil society to stand together against domestic violence and all forms of gender-based violence.","Globally, religious leaders hold unique power to shift community norms. Women's rights groups welcomed the statement — while noting that its real test is whether it translates into action in local communities and courtrooms."]},"body":["穆斯林世界聯盟負責人公開發表聲明，明確表示“針對女性的暴力沒有任何伊斯蘭合法性”。這一表態被外界解讀為伊斯蘭世界權威機構對基於性別暴力的正式劃界。","聲明指出，對婦女的暴力行為既違背伊斯蘭教法的基本原則，也背離伊斯蘭文明對女性尊嚴與權利的長期傳統。聯盟呼籲各國穆斯林學者、宗教機構與社會組織共同反對家庭暴力與一切形式的性別暴力。","在全球範圍內，宗教領袖的立場對改變社群觀念具有獨特影響力。婦女權利組織對此表示歡迎，同時強調：聲明的真正檢驗，在於它能否轉化為各地社區層面的行動與司法實踐。"],"src":"Africa Intelligence","url":"https://www.afintl.com/en/202609111386","region":"中東"}]},{"cat":"文化","en_cat":"Culture","items":[{"id":"001-12","img":"assets/img/womens-rights.png?v=3","t":"第83屆威尼斯電影節：梅爾·圖琪憑《女人，未知》摘金獅","d":"丹麥導演梅爾·圖琪成為史上第八位獲金獅獎的女性電影人，主演瑪蒂爾德·阿塞爾·F.獲最佳女演員獎。授獎辭中她呼籲：照亮共同歷史中那些不為人知的女性。","en":{"t":"Venice 83: May el-Toukhy Wins the Golden Lion for 'The Woman, Unknown'","d":"Danish director May el-Toukhy becomes only the eighth woman to win the Golden Lion; star Mathilde Assef F. takes Best Actress.","body":["On the evening of 12 September, the 83rd Venice Film Festival came to a close on the Lido. The main jury, led by American filmmaker Maggie Gyllenhaal, awarded the Golden Lion to Danish director May el-Toukhy's \"The Woman, Unknown\", with Lee Chang-dong's \"Possible Love\" taking the Grand Jury Prize.","\"The Woman, Unknown\" is the third feature from the Danish-born, Egyptian-descended director. Set around World War II, it follows Marie, a young housekeeper carrying a secret, who is about to marry her wealthy employer — until Denmark's post-war reckoning with \"collaborators\" brings her secret to the surface. Star Mathilde Assef F. also won Best Actress.","Among the 21 films in main competition, \"The Woman, Unknown\" was the only one solely directed by a woman. El-Toukhy becomes only the eighth female filmmaker to win the Golden Lion, after Margarethe von Trotta, Agnès Varda, Sofia Coppola, Chloé Zhao and others. In her speech she was blunt about the industry's unequal treatment of women directors, saying she was driven by \"an urgent need — to illuminate the unknown women of our shared history\"."]},"body":["當地時間9月12日晚，第83屆威尼斯電影節落下帷幕。由美國電影人瑪吉·吉倫哈爾領銜的主競賽評審團，將最高榮譽金獅獎授予丹麥導演梅爾·圖琪（May el-Toukhy）的《女人，未知》（The Woman, Unknown），韓國導演李滄東憑《可能的愛情》獲評審團大獎。","《女人，未知》是這位丹麥出生的埃及裔導演的第三部劇情長片，故事設定在“二戰”前後的丹麥：懷有秘密的年輕女管家瑪麗準備嫁給富有僱主，而戰後對“通敵者”的清算讓她的秘密逐漸浮出水面。影片主演瑪蒂爾德·阿塞爾·F.同時摘得最佳女演員獎。","本屆主競賽21部入圍影片中，《女人，未知》是唯一完全出自女性導演之手的作品。梅爾·圖琪由此成為繼瑪格麗特·馮·特羅塔、阿涅斯·瓦爾達、索菲亞·科波拉、趙婷等人之後，第八位獲金獅獎的女性電影人。授獎辭中她直言行業對女性電影人機會的不公，並說自己堅持的動力是“一種迫切的需要——去照亮我們共同歷史中那些不為人知的女性”。"],"src":"澎湃新聞","url":"https://m.thepaper.cn/detail/34060150","region":"歐洲"},{"id":"001-13","t":"木心美術館年度特展“回望張愛玲”","d":"以手稿、影像與裝置，回望這位影響幾代讀者的女作家。","en":{"t":"Muxin Art Museum's Annual Exhibition Looks Back at Eileen Chang","d":"Manuscripts, films and installations revisit the woman writer who shaped generations of readers.","body":["The Muxin Art Museum's 2026 annual exhibition, \"Looking Back at Eileen Chang\", has opened. Through manuscripts, photographs, film clips and installations, it revisits the writer who shaped generations of readers — from the literary world of \"Love in a Fallen City\" and \"The Golden Cangue\" to her dual bonds with Shanghai and Hong Kong.","The curators aim to show a three-dimensional Chang: not only the cool, bleak novelist, but a sharp essayist, translator and screenwriter. The exhibition highlights her 1940s film scripts, restoring a dimension long overshadowed by her identity as a novelist.","In an era when women's writing is being rediscovered and revalued, the exhibition is both a tribute to one writer and a reaffirmation of a female tradition in Chinese-language literature."]},"body":["木心美術館2026年度特展“回望張愛玲”近日開展。展覽以手稿、照片、影像與裝置等多種媒介，回望這位影響了幾代讀者的女作家——從《傾城之戀》《金鎖記》的文學世界，到其與上海、香港兩座城市的雙重羈絆。","策展方試圖呈現一個“立體”的張愛玲：不只是冷峻蒼涼的小說家，也是敏銳的散文家、譯者與電影編劇。展覽特別梳理了她1940年代的電影劇本創作，還原一個長期被“小說家”身份遮蔽的張愛玲。","在一個女性書寫被重新發現與重估的時代，“回望張愛玲”既是對一位作家的紀念，也是一次對華語文學女性傳統的重新確認。"],"src":"展訊","url":"https://www.sohu.com/a/1074271399_100152450","region":"中國"}]},{"cat":"科技與公益","en_cat":"Tech & Philanthropy","items":[{"id":"001-14","t":"中國婦基會啟動“木蘭AI健康計劃”","d":"中國婦女發展基金會發起“木蘭AI健康計劃”，並參與發佈“我們WOMEN·AI”倡議，推動AI技術惠及女性健康。","en":{"t":"China Women's Development Foundation Launches 'Mulan AI Health Programme'","d":"The foundation launches an AI-driven women's health programme and joins the 'We WOMEN·AI' initiative.","body":["The China Women's Development Foundation has announced the \"Mulan AI Health Programme\" and joined the launch of the \"We WOMEN·AI\" initiative. The programme aims to use artificial intelligence to make health services more accessible for women, especially in grassroots and remote areas — from screening and health literacy to navigation of care.","The initiative also pushes in a second direction: bringing more women into the AI industry itself. Organisers argue that technology built without women's participation can hardly be expected to answer women's needs.","As AI adoption accelerates in 2026, pairing \"tech for good\" with \"tech for women\" is emerging as a new direction in Chinese philanthropy."]},"body":["中國婦女發展基金會宣佈啟動“木蘭AI健康計劃”，並參與發佈“我們WOMEN·AI”倡議。計劃旨在利用人工智能技術，提升女性尤其是基層與偏遠地區女性的健康服務可及性：從健康篩查、疾病科普到就醫導引，AI被設計為“最後一公里”的助手。","倡議同時關注兩個面向：一是讓AI成為女性健康的工具，二是讓更多女性進入AI行業、參與技術的定義。主辦方認為，缺乏女性參與的技術，天然難以回應女性需求。","在AI應用加速落地的2026年，“技術向善”與“技術向女”的結合，正在成為中國公益領域的新方向之一。"],"src":"澎湃新聞","url":"https://m.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_34084972","region":"中國"}]},{"cat":"體育","en_cat":"Sports","items":[{"id":"001-15","t":"女子板球亞洲盃上演印巴對決","d":"2026女子板球亞洲盃印度對陣巴基斯坦的焦點戰引發廣泛關注，女選手表現持續點亮賽場。","en":{"t":"Women's Asia Cup: India–Pakistan Clash Lights Up the Tournament","d":"The India–Pakistan showdown at the 2026 Women's Asia Cup drew wide attention as women cricketers continue to shine.","body":["The 2026 Women's Asia Cup staged its most-watched fixture: India versus Pakistan. Beyond the rivalry, the match extended the rapid rise of women's cricket across the region.","The star power of players such as Indian captain Harmanpreet Kaur has pushed ticket sales and broadcast numbers to new highs, while the professionalisation of women's teams across Asia is taking the game to wider audiences.","From stands to screens, the commercial value of women's sport is being repriced — and behind it all, countless girls now have the option of becoming professional athletes."]},"body":["2026女子板球亞洲盃迎來最受關注的一場較量：印度對陣巴基斯坦。這場焦點戰不僅是兩隊實力的直接對話，更延續了女子板球近年快速升溫的熱度。","印度隊隊長哈曼普麗特·考爾等明星球員的號召力，讓女子板球的票房與轉播數據連創新高。亞洲多國女隊的職業化進程，正在把這項運動帶向更廣闊的觀眾。","從看臺到屏幕，女子體育的商業價值正在被重新定價——而這背後，是無數女孩第一次擁有了“成為職業運動員”的選項。"],"src":"Sandesh","url":"https://sandesh.com/cricket/news/india-vs-pakistan-womens-asia-cup-harmanpreet-kaur","region":"南亞"}]}]}];